            <ArticleTitle>Holt-Oram syndrome: Anesthetic challenges and safe outcome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>110-111</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/0971-9784.197849</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Holt-Oram syndrome (HOS) is an autosomal dominant disease with skeletal and cardiac manifestations. We here are presenting a 31-year-old man and a diagnosed case of HOS, with an ulceroproliferative lesion on lateral border of the tongue, was posted for wide excision of lesion with primary closure and left side radical neck dissection.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
